  <ym-title|Selected tree curvature covariance \V draft
  evidence><label|selected-tree-curvature-covariance--draft-evidence>

  Parent-authored within confirmed issue #26 claim, session
  <verbatim|hairer-codex-existence-20261111>, expiry 2026-11-12 16:40 UTC.
  Source revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. Owned
  text: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/actual-reader-tree-covariance.tex>.
  Status: draft; submitted to independent-review agent for both mathematical
  and Lean correspondence review. No self-approval and no metadata approval.

  <section|Source correspondence><label|source-correspondence>

  All paths below are below <verbatim|Lean/YM/>. The relevant declarations
  and their immediate definitions were read in full, except Station/Affine
  where targeted definition and derivative portions were read. No whole
  source-tree read.

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  step>>|<cell|<strong|Fully qualified declarations>>|<cell|<strong|Path>>>|<row|<cell|Counting
  colour coordinates, full and compressed precision, positive slice
  gap>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.FreeResolvent.{tensor,baseMatrix,fullMatrix,treeMatrix,tree_gap,treeFare}>>|<cell|<verbatim|Push/FREE_RESOLVENT/Flat.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Actual
  flat path-row identification>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.FreeResolvent.Affine.{identity_track,identifies,channel_qf,channels,duct_zero,pulled_inner}>>|<cell|<verbatim|Push/FREE_RESOLVENT/AffineGap.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Channel
  and normalized channel average>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.FreeResolvent.Affine.{tracks,channel,block,primary}>>|<cell|<verbatim|Push/FREE_RESOLVENT/Affine.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Root-pinned
  forest projection and slice inverse>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.FreeResolvent.{potential,representative,roots_pinned,onto_slice,fixes,invariant,treeInverse,covariance,block_solve}>>|<cell|<verbatim|Push/FREE_RESOLVENT/GaugeProjection.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Curvature
  solve without a full potential inverse>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Current.{right_of_count,holder,holder_value,copper,flux_psd,flux_symm,learned}>>|<cell|<verbatim|AnalyticBridge/LOCAL_GAUSSIAN_LAWS/Flux.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Coarse
  column, curvature intertwiner and stationary
  equation>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Current.{psi,neuron,spins,fires}>>|<cell|<verbatim|AnalyticBridge/LOCAL_GAUSSIAN_LAWS/TellerFold.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Cross
  covariance, curl equation and final equality>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.AnalyticBridge.LocalGaussianLaws.Current.{crossed,through,fConditional,plane,cutHead,conditional_psd}>>|<cell|same>>|<row|<cell|Root-corrected
  predictor>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Precision.{fixRoot,mean,probe,psi_proj,root_gradient}>>|<cell|<verbatim|PREC/FrameResponse.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Straightened
  stationary column>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Precision.{straighten,extracted,centers,stays,Inputs,stationed}>>|<cell|<verbatim|PREC/TreeMatch.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Meaning
  of metric/diagonal/attached hypotheses>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Precision.{Bed,Attached,Floor,Towers.Diagonal}>>|<cell|<verbatim|PREC/Stacks.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Signed
  curl invariance and geometric hypotheses>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Bid.{pulled,Sworn,Larger}>>|<cell|<verbatim|Bid/Station.lean>>>>>>

  Notation: manuscript <verbatim|D,D'> are fine/coarse <verbatim|d 1>;
  <verbatim|d_f,d_c> are <verbatim|d 0>; <verbatim|Q> is <verbatim|probe>,
  not <verbatim|mean>; <verbatim|R_0> is <verbatim|fixRoot>;
  <verbatim|M_f,M_c> are <strong|metric> operators; <verbatim|H_f,H_c> are
  <strong|diagonal> operators. The identities used to define <verbatim|J> are
  <verbatim|Floor.diagonalInv> and <verbatim|Towers.Diagonal.stays>. The
  latter does not justify replacing a metric everywhere by a diagonal
  operator. <verbatim|W> is the <verbatim|extracted> installed
  <verbatim|Towers.A0> column. <verbatim|X> is the zero-extended actual tree
  inverse, not a Moore\UPenrose inverse.

  <section|Canonical reuse and boundary><label|canonical-reuse-and-boundary>

  Reuses predictor-branch, seed-tree-patch and sector-gram for the actual
  predictor derivative and flat tree link inequality; uses the already
  constructed same precision tower rather than another free model. The finite
  algebra follows the main steps of <verbatim|Affine.identifies> and
  <verbatim|Current.cutHead>. The elementary range/kernel argument in Flux
  and the stationarity calculation are proved explicitly; no external theorem
  is used in their place. Shared literature index and local Gaussian
  references were searched; no matching recorded source was found that would
  simplify this source-specific tree/covariance identification. No claim of
  novelty.

  The section retains same-bed path attachment, absolute path bounds,
  factorization, signed symmetry, positive floors, predictor branches,
  geometric side conditions and both stationary tower identities. It
  establishes the exact algebraic identification, not production of all those
  hypotheses on the selected public history. It also does not replace the
  separate small-window posed-field comparison or the reference cutoff error.
  Those use canonical local inverse/residual estimates and the narrow bridge
  assigned to lattice-draft. No separate Gaussian reader sampling or omission
  of harmonic potential directions is allowed.

  <section|Checks><label|checks>

  Targeted <verbatim|rg>, <verbatim|cat>, and <verbatim|sed> inspections
  recorded in the parent session. No Lean commands, axiom replay, or source
  edits. No LaTeX build yet for this new file; the preceding 734-page build
  does not include it. Independent review is pending. Structural check to be
  run on integration.

